{"status":"completed","summary":"Provisioned a 1 GiB LUKS1 encrypted XFS volume on node1, mounted at /srv/secure. It automatically unlocked and mounted after a verified node reboot, with test data preserved.","actions_performed":["Installed cryptsetup 2.0.3 from a signature-verified CentOS 7 package matching the existing libraries.","Generated a root-only random key at /root/.secure-volume.key.","Created /var/lib/secure-volume.img and encrypted it with LUKS1.","Created the secure_crypt mapping, formatted it as XFS, and mounted it at /srv/secure.","Configured automatic unlock in /etc/crypttab and automatic mounting in /etc/fstab.","Cold-tested systemd reconstruction after manually closing the mapping.","Restarted node1 and verified the changed boot identity, automatic unlock, mount recovery, and retained data."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure","command_ids":["cmd-84076e835cbc41bb","cmd-1e67a2bcb92d4403"],"summary":"Shows the LUKS container identity and permissions, active dm-crypt mapping, XFS mount, and readable persistence marker."},{"requirement":"Volume unlocks and mounts automatically","command_ids":["cmd-02d948884a12499a","cmd-d8e9cfa26f294c56","cmd-5b2a0c0668d44bc0"],"summary":"Shows crypttab/fstab configuration, successful cold systemd activation, and boot-journal records confirming automatic cryptsetup and mounting."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-97ed7d9270f74fba","cmd-f58bcd5e6a2f4bf0","cmd-e46ce0bcccbe4ee6","cmd-5b2a0c0668d44bc0"],"summary":"Captures the healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, reboot acknowledgement, new boot ID, active encryption and mount units, recovered XFS mount, and unchanged data checksum/content."}]}
